 CellLabel->"In[1]:=",
 CellID->904125756,ExpressionUUID->"8ad9d452-2e30-4456-a46b-e0afaf4735f7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Right contraction is a kind of inner product of multivectors a and b.  If \
grade(b) >  grade(a)  the result is multivector of grade(b) - grade(a) and \
zero otherwise. The StandardForm notation is \[RightContract] (unicode char \
\\ :0x23A3). For input use keyboard alias \[EscapeKey]ir\[EscapeKey] \
(memorize as \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]",
 StyleBox["i",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 "nner ",
 StyleBox["r",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 "ight\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]).  UnicodeSymbols.tr defines the following \
operation precedences: NonCommutativeMultiply (**, highest), Times (*, \
Space), RightContract (\[RightContract]), LeftContract (\[LeftContract]), \
InnerProduct (\[InnerProduct]), CommutativeProduct (\[CommutativeProduct]), \
OuterProduct (\[OuterProduct]), GeometricProduct(\[GeometricProduct]), Plus \
(lowest). To demonstrate the action let\[CloseCurlyQuote]s define some basis \
and two general \nmultivectors ",
 StyleBox["mva", "CodeText"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["mvb", "CodeText"]
}], "Text",
 Editable->True,
